    "explanation": "To both parties: the charge for trip TRP-02824 (RDR-09824 / DRV-09824) is partly refunded.\n\nWHAT THE RECORD SHOWS. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02824) is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 131 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so none of limbs (a) to (c) fires. (The schema pre-pass also tagged it COMPLETE, so there is no schema impairment and no policy impairment — the two are stated separately as POL-GEN-02 and POL-RD-07 require.) The trace measures the trip at 14.4 km (trace_distance_km, the governing field under POL-RD-01). The booked optimal route on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02824) is 2.4 km. The excess is therefore 12.0 km, 500% of optimal: both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km) and the excess also clears the materiality gate (greater than 50% and greater than 8.0 km). The deviation is ESTABLISHED and MATERIAL, corroborated by the trip record's own optimal-distance field, which is a platform routing-engine estimate rather than a copy of the trace.\n\nNO EXONERATION. The driver's statement in the dispute record — that the rider changed the destination verbally — is an assertion that cites no evidence ID; under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and is discarded. It is also contradicted in form by the record: the chat log for this trip (EV-CHAT-02824) contains 0 messages, so there is no recorded rider instruction, no waypoint_hint and no named road. POL-RD-04 cannot be satisfied and, as that clause directs, its corroboration test could not be run; the case is decided on the remaining clauses. POL-RD-05 cannot re-baseline the route either: original_pickup, original_dropoff, pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are all null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so there is no amended endpoint to re-quote against. The only advisory artifact (EV-ADVIS-02824-01) is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and no payload, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no external traffic cause can reduce the excess; under POL-RD-13 that absence is a gap in the bundle (the driver named no advisory ID), not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The vehicle type is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-12 does not apply.\n\nTHE REFUND. fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 runs and the refund is arithmetic. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 2.4 km + 0.28 x 5.0 min) x 1.0 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 waiting fee - 0 promo = 7.80. The surge multiplier of 1.0 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, not from the trip record. Charged_total is 21.48. Refund = 21.48 - 7.80 = 13.68, rounded UP to SGD 13.70. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and at 63.7% of charged_total it is below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND, not a FULL_REFUND.\n\nPASS-THROUGH LINES. The fare breakdown carries no ERP gantry lines, no airport surcharge, no tolls and no waiting-time fee, and the trip neither originates nor ends at an airport. POL-RD-09 therefore adds nothing on top of the POL-RD-02 figure and nothing is double-counted.\n\nNO DRIVER UPLIFT OR REFERRAL. Because the deviation is MATERIAL, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check was run: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 210 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established. There is no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). No other referral is produced by any clause: there are no unmatched charge lines (POL-RD-09(4)) and no false-arrival record (POL-NS-05(ii)). Profile fields outside the citable counters (ratings, active_region, lifetime counters) were treated as context only under POL-GEN-01 and grounded nothing.\n\nNEXT STEP. The monetary effect of SGD 13.70 exceeds the execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this provisional ruling is issued but not executed: the amount is held and the case is placed in the human queue for release under POL-GEN-05. Either party may appeal within 30 days under POL-GEN-04.\n\nConfidence: 0.9. The deciding facts (the 14.4 km trace measurement, the 2.4 km booked optimal, and the fare arithmetic) are carried by EV-GPS-02824, EV-TRIP-02824 and EV-FARE-02824, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so nothing below weight 1.0 carries the ruling and the cap is not depressed; the residual discount reflects the unverifiable verbal-destination-change assertion, which the record cannot test."
