    "explanation": "Both of you: the trip booked as a 2.4 km run between Blk 55 Lengkok Bahru and Blk 25 Ghim Moh Link was driven as 14.4 km, and nothing on the record justifies the extra 12.0 km.\n\nThe deviation. The GPS trace for TRP-02824 (EV-GPS-02824) is the governing measurement under POL-RD-01 and shows 14.4 km against the 2.4 km platform optimal, an excess of 12.0 km, or 500%. Both establishment tests pass (over 20% of optimal and over 0.8 km absolute) and the excess also clears the materiality gate (over 50% and over 8.0 km), so the deviation is established and material. The trace is clean for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 131 fixes, 10-second sampling, 100% coverage, zero gaps and a max gap of 0.0 seconds, so no limb of (a) to (c) fires and the deviation stands on the trace alone without independent corroboration.\n\nThe money. The fare is METERED, so POL-RD-02 applies and the refund is arithmetic. recomputed_fare = (3.80 base fare + 0.75 x 2.4 km = 1.80 distance + 0.28 x 5.0 min = 1.40 time) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee, plus 0 ERP, plus 0 waiting time, less 0 promo = 7.80. charged_total is 21.48. Refund = 21.48 - 7.80 = 13.68, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05, giving SGD 13.70. That is 63.7% of the charge: above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 13.70.\n\nThe driver's explanation. The statement that the rider changed the destination verbally is an assertion with no artifact behind it. The chat log for this trip (EV-CHAT-02824) is complete and contains zero messages, so there is no rider instruction, no waypoint_hint and no named road: POL-RD-04 cannot be run and its corroboration test cannot even be reached. The trip record shows original pickup and dropoff, and the amendment timestamps, all null with amended_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run either. Under POL-RD-08 an assertion that points to no evidence carries no weight, and the excess is not reduced. The rider's profile does not add any corroboration burden (deviation_claims_60d = 1, below the threshold of 4).\n\nTraffic. No traffic advisory covers this trip. The only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-02824-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and, under POL-RD-13, no external-cause explanation reduces the excess. Because no advisory identifier was cited by the party asserting an external cause, this is a gap in the bundle rather than the escalation trigger in POL-RD-10(5), and the deviation stands at the measured figure.\n\nProfile and conduct. Because the deviation is material, POL-RD-06 requires the driver profile check: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 210 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no conduct referral follows. No context-only profile field has been used as a ground of decision.\n\nPass-through charges and compensation. The fare breakdown carries 0.00 of ERP, no gantry lines, no airport surcharge and no waiting-time fee, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and nothing is counted twice. The driver is not owed compensation: the billed distance (14.4 km) equals the traced distance, so there is no unbilled-distance shortfall of more than 1.0 km under POL-RD-04.\n\nConfidence and execution. Every artifact carrying the deciding facts - the trace and trip record for the deviation, the fare breakdown for the arithmetic - sits at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is not capped below 1.0; I have set it at 0.90. The ruling moves SGD 13.70, which is above the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it issues but is not executed automatically: the amount is held and the case is placed in the human queue for release. Either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04. For completeness of disclosure, one rider claim was discarded at the citation check for citing the missing advisory without naming its issue code; that discard does not affect the outcome, which rests on the trace and the fare recomputation."
